<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_4_5" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_4_5" name="4.5 Operate mobile devices and reconcile offline work" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>4.5.2 and 4.5.4 are drawn. 4.5.1 offline operation and 4.5.3 map and spatial context are specified without models and correctly so - both are standing device capabilities with no instance boundary. A crew is not 'in' an offline process; the device is either connected or it is not.

SECTION I OF THE SOURCE PACK NAMES THIS AS UNSTANDARDISED. Offline behaviour, sync conflict resolution, field data capture and electronic forms are recorded there as entirely vendor-defined - there is no standard anywhere. So this file draws the ORDER and the CONFLICT ROUTE, which are process facts, and states no resolution rule, which would be a vendor's.

Controlled order matters and is drawn: records transmit in the order they were created, because a completion that arrives before the safety record it depends on produces a work order that looks finished and unsafe. And a conflict is ROUTED rather than auto-resolved - last-write-wins on a field record silently discards what a crew saw.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_4_5_lanes">
      <lane id="l_45_field" name="Field and device">
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_q</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_ack</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_cf</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_d</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_as</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_cfg</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_ref</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_ev</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_resp</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_45_back" name="Back office">
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_route</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_ret</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_end</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_rem</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_45_end2</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_45_start" name="Connectivity is restored"><conditionalEventDefinition id="n_45_start_cd"><condition/></conditionalEventDefinition></startEvent>
    <serviceTask id="n_45_q" name="Transmit pending records in controlled order"><documentation>4.5.2. In creation order. A completion arriving before its safety record produces a work order that reads as finished and unsafe.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <receiveTask id="n_45_ack" name="Confirm receipt and identify conflicts"><documentation>4.5.2.</documentation></receiveTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_45_cf" name="Conflict"/>
    <sendTask id="n_45_route" name="Route each conflict for resolution"><documentation>4.5.2. Routed, never auto-resolved. No source states a resolution rule and last-write-wins discards field observation.</documentation></sendTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_45_ret" name="Retain the synchronisation result"><documentation>4.5.2. Including what did not land - a partial sync that reports success is the failure mode this step exists for.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <endEvent id="n_45_end" name="Field data reconciled"/>
    <startEvent id="n_45_d" name="Device assignment or support request"><messageEventDefinition id="n_45_d_md"/></startEvent>
    <serviceTask id="n_45_as" name="Assign the device to an authorised worker or pool"><documentation>4.5.4. Authorised - 14.1.4 provisions the access this depends on.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_45_cfg" name="Apply approved access and application configuration"><documentation>4.5.4.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_45_ref" name="Confirm required reference data is available"><documentation>4.5.4. What 4.5.1 will run on when the device goes offline - a device provisioned without reference data is a device that cannot work offline.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_45_ev" name="Loss, failure or support request"/>
    <userTask id="n_45_resp" name="Respond to the loss, failure or request"><documentation>4.5.4.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_45_rem" name="Remove access and recover the device"><documentation>4.5.4. At end of assignment, and 14.1.4 de-provisions - a recovered device with live access is the same exposure as a lost one.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <endEvent id="n_45_end2" name="Device managed"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_start_n_45_q" sourceRef="n_45_start" targetRef="n_45_q" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_q_n_45_ack" sourceRef="n_45_q" targetRef="n_45_ack" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_ack_n_45_cf" sourceRef="n_45_ack" targetRef="n_45_cf" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_cf_n_45_route" sourceRef="n_45_cf" targetRef="n_45_route" name="conflict"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[conflict = true]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_route_n_45_ret" sourceRef="n_45_route" targetRef="n_45_ret" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_cf_n_45_ret" sourceRef="n_45_cf" targetRef="n_45_ret" name="clean"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_ret_n_45_end" sourceRef="n_45_ret" targetRef="n_45_end" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_d_n_45_as" sourceRef="n_45_d" targetRef="n_45_as" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_as_n_45_cfg" sourceRef="n_45_as" targetRef="n_45_cfg" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_cfg_n_45_ref" sourceRef="n_45_cfg" targetRef="n_45_ref" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_ref_n_45_ev" sourceRef="n_45_ref" targetRef="n_45_ev" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_ev_n_45_resp" sourceRef="n_45_ev" targetRef="n_45_resp" name="loss, failure or request"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[supportEvent = true]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_resp_n_45_rem" sourceRef="n_45_resp" targetRef="n_45_rem" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_ev_n_45_rem" sourceRef="n_45_ev" targetRef="n_45_rem" name="end of assignment"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_45_rem_n_45_end2" sourceRef="n_45_rem" targetRef="n_45_end2" name=""/>
  </process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="dg_P_4_5">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="pl_P_4_5" bpmnElement="P_4_5">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="sh_n_45_start" bpmnElement="n_45_start"><dc:Bounds x="132" y="217" width="36" height="36"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="sh_n_45_q" bpmnElement="n_45_q"><dc:Bounds x="255" y="191.5" width="130" height="87"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
